<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajaram I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1670–1700</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Chhatrapati Rajaram</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajaram I was the younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhatrapati">Chhatrapati</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> kingdom from 1689 to 1700. After his brother Sambhaji was captured and executed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, he escaped south to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gingee">Gingee</a>, which held out against a long Mughal siege, while Maratha commanders fought on in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. After his death his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarabai">Tarabai</a> led the resistance in the name of their son.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajaram-i.jpg" alt="Rajaram I" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Augustus Kincaid &amp;amp; Dattatray Balwant Parasnis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chhatrapati_Rajaram_Maharaja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
